  "description_html": "Restoration of the ankylosaurid dinosaur <i>Pinacosaurus</i>. \n<ul><li>This restoration was originally uploaded in 2009 as a restoration of the closely related dinosaur <i>Saichania</i>, as it is primarily based on the fossil specimen MPC 100/1305, which at the time was referred to <i>Saichania</i>. MPC 100/1305 have subsequently been re-classified as a <i>Pinacosaurus</i>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"References\">References</h3></div>\n<ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-1\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">Arbour V.M. &amp; Currie P.J. (2013). \"The taxonomic identity of a nearly complete ankylosaurid dinosaur skeleton from the Gobi Desert of Mongolia\". <i>Cretaceous Research</i> <b>46</b>: p. 24-30: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.cretres.2013.08.008\">https://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.cretres.2013.08.008</a></span>\n</li>\n</ol>",
